join detective right
detective: What can you tell me about the guard?
join niece left
niece: They were as diligent a guard as I’ve ever seen.
niece: I kept insisting that they come in for a bite to eat, but they refused.
niece: It’s rather noble of them, I suppose, but I just felt awful seeing them out in the cold for so long!
niece: My uncle did bring them inside for a tour around the place at one point, but that didn't last for very long, and they were right back outside after.
niece: Even after my poor uncle had passed out, and Aslan was busy berating the cook, they wouldn't listen to me asking them to come in.
niece: When Aslan asked them to come in shortly after that, they finally obliged.
niece (disappointed): Some people like to play favorites for no reason.
niece (speaking): Together, Andrei and I were the first to see that Dracula had been stabbed.
niece: …except for his murderer, of course.
